// ===== Viewport culling (B) =====================================================================
// The browser laying out + painting every focus node (631 on Armenia, thousands on big trees) is what
// makes zoom/pan janky. Cull: nodes whose box falls outside the visible viewport (+ a margin so panning
// doesn't pop) are display:none'd — removed from layout/paint while staying in the DOM (so node reuse,
// selection state, and the data/save model are all untouched). Re-evaluated on zoom, render, and scroll.
